+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

xandikos listens by default on localhost:8080 without authentication.

It is highly recommended to have it sit behind a reverse proxy which
performs authentication when exposing it to the internet. On OpenBSD,
you can, for example, use relayd(8) as a reverse proxy performing
authentication using TLS client certificates. For more information,
refer to the documentation in relayd.conf(5).
